ng by superimposing waves that  increase in frequency as we add more  tokens  for the third token the frequency of  each wave we add increases even more  like this to put it as an analogy the  new representation of each token  is like a cake where the base  frequency is still the first token then  the second token adds  some detail and becomes the cream on the  cake  then the third token becomes the even  more detailed icing  the fourth token is the super detailed  nuts and so on  and then the whole cake is the new token  representation  because we take the summation of all of  this and to be fair  all of this has real and complex  components but forget about it because  after all the operations are computed  the authors delete the imaginary  component  anyway the important messages here are  firstly  the fourier transform applied to tokens  mixes the tokens among  themselves it's kind of similar to what  self-attention does but self-attention  learned the weights by which these  things need to be mixed  also the same thing is done to the  hidden dimensions  so that the features of the tokens are  also mixed among each other and until  here the transformation that was done  is reversible by the inverse fourier  transform in other words the components  of the cake  can be recovered by decomposing after  each frequency it is  the next step the feed forward layers  that mix  things even more and usually not in  an invertible way the second important  message  is that the mixing scheme or pattern is  not learned it is fixed and always  follows the same rule  making the architecture simpler and  easier to compute  it decreases the number of the learnable  parameters of the transformer  which now is technically ethnic and not  the transformer  thirdly a more advanced taco message  also  mentioned in the paper which miss coffee  bean found super interesting is the  following  you maybe know or if not just take miss  coffee beans word for it  convolutions in the real slash 